{"strongs": "H3541", "word": "כֹּה", "translit": "koh", "root": "כדר", "morph": "H:Adv", "pos": "demonstrative adverb", "gloss": "thus, here", "definition": "כֹּה demonstrative adverb thus, here (Biblical Aramaic כָּה ; ᵑ7 , ᵑ6 :Jerusalem, Mandean כָּא here: in Syriac with prefixes hither , ( ᵑ6 :Jerusalem ) hence , where? compare אֵיכָה , p. 32, and Kö ii. 1, 252 ) — 1. of manner, thus (so most frequently, and usually pointing to what is to follow, while כֵּן points commonly to what has preceded), Gen 15:5 כה יהיה זרעך thus shall thy seed be, Num 6:23 ; 1Kgs 2:30 כֹּה דִבֶּר יוֺאָב וְכֹה עָנָנִי , 1Kgs 5:25 ; Isa 24:13 (answered by בְּ , as Jer 23:29 ); with a substantive Isa 20:6 הִנֵּה כֹה מַבָּטֵנוּ , Jer 9:21 (si vera lectio), Jer 23:29 ; 1Sam 27:11 . Mostly confined to particular phrases: thus \\ \\ a. with different forms of אמר , כה תאמר thus shalt thou say Exod 3:14 ; Exod 3:15 ; Exod 19:3 ; Exod 20:22 etc.; especially כה אמר יי֞ thus saith (or said) ׳ י Exod 4:22 ; Exod 5:1 ; Exod 7:17 ; Exod 7:26 ; Exod 8:16 etc.; and continually in the prophets, as Isa 7:7 ; Isa 8:11 ; Isa 18:4 etc.; Jer 2:2 ; Jer 2:5 ; Jer 4:27 ; Jer 6:16 etc.; also in the idiomatic formula אִם כֹּה יאֹמַר if he say (or used to say ) (the words spoken following) Gen 31:8 ; 1Sam 14:9 ; 1Sam 14:10 ; 1Sam 20:7 ; 2Sam 15:26 . \\ \\ b. with עשׂה to do thus , Exod 5:15 ; Deut 7:5 pointing back, Num 22:30 ; Josh 6:14 ; 1Sam 27:11 and elsewhere; especially in the phrase כה יעשׂה אלהים וכה יוסיף (with variations), 1Sam 3:17 + (see יסף ), in which כֹּה points to an imprecation understood but not expressed. With בְּ prefixed 1Kgs 22:20 ויאמר זה בְּכֹה וזה אמר בְּכֹה and one spake in this wise , and another spake in that wise (|| 2Chr 18:19 כָכָהכָּ֗֗֗כָה ; probably rightly). 2. of place, here (rare, chiefly in E ), Gen 31:37 שִׂים כֹּה place it here before my brethren, Num 23:15 (twice in verse); 2Sam 18:30 ; Ruth 2:8 . Repeated, Exod 2:12 וַיִּפֶן כֹּה וָכֹה and he turned this way and that way ; כֹּהכֹּ֗֗֗ה on this side . . . on that side Num 11:31 . With עַד Gen 22:5 and we will go עַדכֹּֿה as far as here ( δεικτικῶς ) i.e. yonder. 3. of time, עַד כֹּה hitherto , Exod 7:16 (compare עַדהֵֿנָּה ), Josh 17:14 עַדכֹּֿה וְעַדכֹּֿה till now and till then , i.e. meanwhile, 1Kgs 18:45 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3924')\">BDB3924</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H3541')\">H3541</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3923')\">BDB3923</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3925')\">BDB3925</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>כֹּה</bdbheb> <b>demonstrative adverb</b> <highlightword>thus, here</highlightword> (Biblical Aramaic <bdbarc>כָּה</bdbarc>; <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Tg')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ7</reflink></bdbheb></lookup>, <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Syr')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ6</reflink></bdbheb></lookup>:Jerusalem, Mandean <bdbheb>כָּא</bdbheb> <highlight>here:</highlight> in Syriac with prefixes <placeholder2449/> <highlight>hither</highlight>, <placeholder2450/> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Syr')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ6</reflink></bdbheb></lookup>:Jerusalem <placeholder2451/>) <highlight>hence</highlight>, <placeholder2452/> <highlight>where?</highlight> compare <bdbheb>אֵיכָה</bdbheb>, p. 32, and <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Kö')\">Kö<sup>ii. 1, 252</sup></lookup>) — <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> of manner, <highlight>thus</highlight> (so most frequently, and usually pointing to what is to follow, while <bdbheb>כֵּן</bdbheb> points commonly to what has preceded), <ref ref=\"Gen 15:5\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(1,15,5)\">Gen 15:5</ref> <bdbheb>כה יהיה זרעך</bdbheb> <highlight>thus</highlight> shall thy seed be, <ref ref=\"Num 6:23\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(4,6,23)\">Num 6:23</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Kgs 2:30\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"30\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"30\" onclick=\"bcv(11,2,30)\">1Kgs 2:30</ref> <bdbheb>כֹּה דִבֶּר יוֺאָב וְכֹה עָנָנִי</bdbheb>, <ref ref=\"1Kgs 5:25\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(11,5,25)\">1Kgs 5:25</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 24:13\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(23,24,13)\">Isa 24:13</ref> (answered by <bdbheb>בְּ</bdbheb>, as <ref ref=\"Jer 23:29\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(24,23,29)\">Jer 23:29</ref>); with a substantive <ref ref=\"Isa 20:6\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"20\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"20\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(23,20,6)\">Isa 20:6</ref> <bdbheb>הִנֵּה</bdbheb> <bdbheb>כֹה מַבָּטֵנוּ</bdbheb>, <ref ref=\"Jer 9:21\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(24,9,21)\">Jer 9:21</ref> (si vera lectio), <ref ref=\"Jer 23:29\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(24,23,29)\">Jer 23:29</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Sam 27:11\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"27\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"27\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(9,27,11)\">1Sam 27:11</ref>. Mostly confined to particular phrases: thus <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>a.</b> with different forms of <bdbheb>אמר</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>כה תאמר</bdbheb> <highlight>thus</highlight> shalt thou say <ref ref=\"Exod 3:14\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(2,3,14)\">Exod 3:14</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 3:15\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(2,3,15)\">Exod 3:15</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 19:3\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(2,19,3)\">Exod 19:3</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 20:22\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"20\" vBegin=\"22\" cEnd=\"20\" vEnd=\"22\" onclick=\"bcv(2,20,22)\">Exod 20:22</ref> etc.; especially <bdbheb>כה אמר יי֞</bdbheb> thus saith (or said) <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>י</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Exod 4:22\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"22\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"22\" onclick=\"bcv(2,4,22)\">Exod 4:22</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 5:1\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(2,5,1)\">Exod 5:1</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 7:17\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(2,7,17)\">Exod 7:17</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 7:26\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"26\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"26\" onclick=\"bcv(2,7,26)\">Exod 7:26</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 8:16\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(2,8,16)\">Exod 8:16</ref> etc.; and continually in the prophets, as <ref ref=\"Isa 7:7\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(23,7,7)\">Isa 7:7</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 8:11\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(23,8,11)\">Isa 8:11</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 18:4\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(23,18,4)\">Isa 18:4</ref> etc.; <ref ref=\"Jer 2:2\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(24,2,2)\">Jer 2:2</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 2:5\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(24,2,5)\">Jer 2:5</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 4:27\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"27\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"27\" onclick=\"bcv(24,4,27)\">Jer 4:27</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 6:16\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(24,6,16)\">Jer 6:16</ref> etc.; also in the idiomatic formula <bdbheb>אִם כֹּה יאֹמַר</bdbheb> <highlight>if he say</highlight> (or <highlight>used to say</highlight>) (the words spoken following) <ref ref=\"Gen 31:8\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(1,31,8)\">Gen 31:8</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Sam 14:9\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(9,14,9)\">1Sam 14:9</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Sam 14:10\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(9,14,10)\">1Sam 14:10</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Sam 20:7\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"20\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"20\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(9,20,7)\">1Sam 20:7</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Sam 15:26\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"26\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"26\" onclick=\"bcv(10,15,26)\">2Sam 15:26</ref>. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>b.</b> with <bdbheb>עשׂה</bdbheb> to do <highlight>thus</highlight>, <ref ref=\"Exod 5:15\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(2,5,15)\">Exod 5:15</ref>; <ref ref=\"Deut 7:5\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(5,7,5)\">Deut 7:5</ref> pointing back, <ref ref=\"Num 22:30\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"22\" vBegin=\"30\" cEnd=\"22\" vEnd=\"30\" onclick=\"bcv(4,22,30)\">Num 22:30</ref>; <ref ref=\"Josh 6:14\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(6,6,14)\">Josh 6:14</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Sam 27:11\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"27\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"27\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(9,27,11)\">1Sam 27:11</ref> and elsewhere; especially in the phrase <bdbheb>כה יעשׂה אלהים וכה יוסיף</bdbheb> (with variations), <ref ref=\"1Sam 3:17\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(9,3,17)\">1Sam 3:17</ref> + (see  <bdbheb><reflink>יסף</reflink></bdbheb>), in which <bdbheb>כֹּה</bdbheb> points to an imprecation understood but not expressed. With <bdbheb>בְּ</bdbheb> prefixed <ref ref=\"1Kgs 22:20\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"22\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"22\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(11,22,20)\">1Kgs 22:20</ref> <bdbheb>ויאמר זה בְּכֹה וזה אמר בְּכֹה</bdbheb> and one spake <highlight>in this wise</highlight>, and another spake <highlight>in that wise</highlight> (|| <ref ref=\"2Chr 18:19\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(14,18,19)\">2Chr 18:19</ref> <bdbheb>כָכָהכָּ֗֗֗כָה</bdbheb>; probably rightly). </div><div class=\"point\"><b>2.</b> of place, <highlight>here</highlight> (rare, chiefly in <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('E')\"><reflink>E</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"Gen 31:37\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"37\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"37\" onclick=\"bcv(1,31,37)\">Gen 31:37</ref> <bdbheb>שִׂים כֹּה</bdbheb> place it <highlight>here</highlight> before my brethren, <ref ref=\"Num 23:15\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(4,23,15)\">Num 23:15</ref> (twice in verse); <ref ref=\"2Sam 18:30\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"30\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"30\" onclick=\"bcv(10,18,30)\">2Sam 18:30</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ruth 2:8\" b=\"8\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(8,2,8)\">Ruth 2:8</ref>. Repeated, <ref ref=\"Exod 2:12\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(2,2,12)\">Exod 2:12</ref> <bdbheb>וַיִּפֶן כֹּה וָכֹה</bdbheb> and he turned <highlight>this way</highlight> and <highlight>that way</highlight>; <bdbheb>כֹּהכֹּ֗֗֗ה</bdbheb> <highlight>on this side . . . on that side</highlight> <ref ref=\"Num 11:31\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"31\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"31\" onclick=\"bcv(4,11,31)\">Num 11:31</ref>. With <bdbheb>עַד</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 22:5\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"22\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"22\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(1,22,5)\">Gen 22:5</ref> and we will go <bdbheb>עַדכֹּֿה</bdbheb> <highlight>as far as here</highlight> (<grk>δεικτικῶς</grk>) i.e. <highlight>yonder.</highlight> </div><div class=\"point\"><b>3.</b> of time, <bdbheb>עַד כֹּה</bdbheb> <highlight>hitherto</highlight>, <ref ref=\"Exod 7:16\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(2,7,16)\">Exod 7:16</ref> (compare <bdbheb>עַדהֵֿנָּה</bdbheb>), <ref ref=\"Josh 17:14\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(6,17,14)\">Josh 17:14</ref> <bdbheb>עַדכֹּֿה</bdbheb> <bdbheb>וְעַדכֹּֿה</bdbheb> till <highlight>now</highlight> and till <highlight>then</highlight>, i.e. meanwhile, <ref ref=\"1Kgs 18:45\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"45\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"45\" onclick=\"bcv(11,18,45)\">1Kgs 18:45</ref>. </p></div><hr>", "references": [{"raw": "Gen 15:5", "book": "GEN", "chapter": 15, "verse": 5}, {"raw": "Num 6:23", "book": "NUM", "chapter": 6, "verse": 23}, {"raw"